    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n57939" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κλῑν-ικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of</i> or <i>for a bed</i>: as Subst.,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κλινικός, ὁ</span>, <i>physician who visits his patients in their
				beds</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				12.829
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				11.113
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Nicarch.
			</span></i>); title of work by Damocrates, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				13.349
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ -κή</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέχνη</span>) <i>his art</i> or
			<i>method</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plin.
				<u>HN</u>
				29.4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>bed-ridden</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γέρων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aus.
					<u>Ep.</u>
					8.34
				</span></i>
			.</div>
